<title>USA: Coastal USG rigs back up after Hurricane.</title>
<headline>Coastal USG rigs back up after Hurricane.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coastal Corp has returned its offshore production platforms in the Gulf of Mexico back to service following shut ins late last week ahead of Hurricane Danny, Coastal spokesman Brian Mitchell said.</p>
<p>&quot;All our offshore is back up,&quot; Mitchell said.</p>
<p>Mitchell said Coastal shut in about 100 million cubic feet of natural gas production and just under 5,000 barrels of condensate from two platforms as Hurricane Danny stormed through the central U.S. Gulf.</p>
<p>((-- New York Oil Desk 1 212 859 1633))</p>
